    "featuredImage": "/images/karachi-metropolitan-university-vc-2026.webp",
    "imageAlt": "Karachi Metropolitan University KMU Vice Chancellor Recruitment 2026 Sindh",
    "excerpt": "The Government of Sindh Universities & Boards Department has announced the statutory recruitment of Vice Chancellor for Karachi Metropolitan University (KMU). Applications are invited through the Search Committee by 29 October 2026.",
    "content": [
      "### Statutory Leadership Announcement: Vice Chancellor Karachi Metropolitan University",
      "The **Universities & Boards Department, Government of Sindh**, through its statutory **Search Committee**, has officially issued a public advertisement inviting applications from eminent scholars, researchers, and academic administrators for the prestigious position of **Vice Chancellor at Karachi Metropolitan University (KMU)**.",
      "Chartered as a premier public-sector higher education institution in Karachi, Karachi Metropolitan University provides multidisciplinary academic, medical, and technological education. The search for a regular Vice Chancellor was initiated following the appointment of KMU’s founding Vice Chancellor, Prof. Dr. Wasim Qazi, as the Vice Chancellor of the University of Karachi in October 2026.",
      "This statutory appointment will be made for a **four-year tenure** by the Honourable Chief Minister of Sindh upon the formal recommendations of the Search Committee, in accordance with the Sindh Public Sector Universities Laws and Higher Education Commission (HEC) guidelines.",
      "### Quick Summary Table: KMU Vice Chancellor Recruitment",
      "| Metric / Parameter | Statutory Specification |\n|:---|:---|\n| **Appointing Authority** | Chief Minister of Sindh on Search Committee Recommendations |\n| **Administrative Department** | Universities & Boards Department, Government of Sindh |\n| **Target Institution** | Karachi Metropolitan University (KMU), Karachi |\n| **Statutory Post** | Vice Chancellor (Chief Executive & Academic Officer) |\n| **Tenure of Appointment** | 4-Year Fixed Term (Extendable for one additional term per law) |\n| **Minimum Academic Qualification** | Ph.D. or Equivalent Terminal Degree (HEC / PMDC Recognized) |\n| **Experience Benchmark** | 15–20 Years of Distinguished Teaching, Research & University Administration |\n| **Age Limit** | Maximum 62 Years as on Closing Date |\n| **Publication Date** | 14 October 2026 |\n| **Application Deadline** | **29 October 2026** |\n| **Official Department Portal** | [universitiesboards.sindh.gov.pk](https://universitiesboards.sindh.gov.pk/) |",
      "### Mandatory Eligibility & Selection Criteria",
      "Candidates applying for the leadership of Karachi Metropolitan University must satisfy rigorous academic and managerial criteria:",
      "1. **Academic Credentials:** Distinguished academic record with a Ph.D. or terminal doctorate (or equivalent recognized medical terminal qualification such as FCPS/MD/MS where applicable) from a reputable, HEC-recognized national or foreign university.\n2. **Research Track Record:** A substantial portfolio of quality research publications indexed in HEC-recognized high-impact journals, alongside proven experience guiding post-graduate research.\n3. **Administrative & Financial Leadership:** Minimum 15 to 20 years of demonstrable experience in higher education, including senior leadership roles (such as Dean, Director, Registrar, or Head of Department), with proven competence in institutional governance, budget oversight, and endowment development.\n4. **Strategic Vision:** Demonstrated capacity to foster academic industry linkages, international collaborations, accreditation compliance, and modern campus infrastructure.\n5. **Age Limit:** The applicant must not have exceeded **62 years of age** on the official closing date of applications (**29 October 2026**).",
      "### Step-by-Step Application & Submission Instructions",
      "Eminent candidates desiring to serve as the Vice Chancellor of Karachi Metropolitan University must adhere to the formal submission workflow:",
      "1. **Obtain Official Guidelines:** Review the complete vacancy announcement on the official portal of the [Universities & Boards Department](https://universitiesboards.sindh.gov.pk/jobs).\n2. **Prepare Professional Portfolio:** Compile a comprehensive Curriculum Vitae detailing academic qualifications, chronologically listed employment history, administrative appointments, research publications with impact factors, and citations.\n3. **Institutional Vision Statement:** Prepare a succinct strategic vision statement (not exceeding 1,000 words) outlining priorities for transforming Karachi Metropolitan University into a top-tier research and innovation hub.\n4. **Supporting Documents:** Attach verified copies of degrees, HEC equivalence, CNIC, and recent passport-sized photographs.\n5. **Delivery Address:** Submit the sealed dossier marked *\"Application for the Post of Vice Chancellor, Karachi Metropolitan University\"* to the Secretary, Universities & Boards Department, Government of Sindh, Karachi, on or before **29 October 2026**.",
      "### Editorial & Transparency Standards",
      "CareerDost reports public appointments and higher education leadership notices with strict journalistic fidelity:\n- **Government Non-Affiliation:** CareerDost is an independent informational publication and has no role in candidate screening or interview shortlisting. Review our public mission on the [CareerDost About & Editorial Policy](/about#editorial-policy).\n- **Zero-Fee Policy:** The Government of Sindh does not solicit payments through unverified private intermediaries for statutory higher education appointments.",
      "### Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)",
      "**Q1: What is the tenure of the Vice Chancellor at Karachi Metropolitan University?**  \nThe Vice Chancellor is appointed for a statutory tenure of four (4) years by the Chief Minister of Sindh on the recommendation of the Search Committee.\n\n**Q2: What is the maximum age limit for applying?**  \nThe candidate must be 62 years of age or younger on 29 October 2026.\n\n**Q3: Why was the Vice Chancellor post re-advertised for KMU?**  \nThe vacancy arose following the transfer and appointment of founding Vice Chancellor Prof. Dr. Wasim Qazi to lead the University of Karachi as Vice Chancellor."
    ],
