    "logoInitial": "SKS",
    "featuredImage": "/images/sindh-kisan-subsidy-2026-eligibility-payments.webp",
    "imageAlt": "Sindh Kisan Subsidy 2026 25 Acre Farmers Eligibility and Payment Guide",
    "excerpt": "Detailed breakdown of the Sindh Cabinet wheat relief decision for farmers owning up to 25 acres. Learn the rules for fresh registration, revalidation of past beneficiaries, Form VII checks, and Sindh Bank payments.",
    "content": [
      "# Sindh Kisan Subsidy 2026: 25 Acre Tak Farmers Ke Liye Registration Aur Payment Rules",
      "> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Editorial Notice — Cross-Reference & Merge Advisory:**\n> This article focuses specifically on the **Sindh Cabinet's policy decisions and payment rules** reported via official state media (APP). Because this policy represents the legislative basis of the **Sindh Wheat Growers Support Program**, readers can find the comprehensive operational guide in our master article: [Sindh Wheat Subsidy 2026: Benazir Hari Card Registration Update](https://careerdost.blog/jobs/sindh-wheat-subsidy-benazir-hari-card-2026).",
      "## Cabinet Approval: The 25-Acre Framework",
      "The Sindh Cabinet, in its recent session chaired by Chief Minister Syed Murad Ali Shah, formally ratified a comprehensive relief package for provincial wheat cultivators for the 2026–27 season.\n\nThe policy specifically caps financial assistance at **25 acres**, aiming to direct state resources to subsistence growers who bear the brunt of inflation in fuel, fertilizer, and agricultural chemicals.",
      "## Key Rules: New Registration vs. Revalidation",
      "To ensure fiscal transparency and eliminate duplicate payments, the cabinet mandated a strict verification protocol administered through the Revenue Department and Directorate General Agriculture Extension:\n\n1. **Revalidation of Existing Beneficiaries:** Farmers who enrolled during earlier relief cycles must undergo data revalidation to verify continued cultivation and active land status.\n2. **Fresh Registration of Unenrolled Growers:** Eligible smallholders not yet registered must present their land title (Form VII) or registered tenancy deeds before local scrutiny committees.\n3. **Elimination of Intermediaries:** Under no circumstances will manual vouchers or cash distributions be permitted. All payouts are funneled through digital accounts.",
      "## Payment Mechanism via Sindh Bank & Hari Card",
      "The disbursement workflow approved by the provincial cabinet operates as follows:\n- **Account Opening:** Eligible farmers are provided designated accounts at **Sindh Bank** linked with biometric verification.\n- **Benazir Hari Card Issuance:** Cardholders receive a customized debit card enabling direct cash withdrawals at ATMs or branch point-of-sale (POS) terminals.\n- **Direct Electronic Credit:** Subsidies for inputs such as DAP are credited via electronic funds transfer upon department authorization.",
      "## Unconfirmed Disbursement Dates: What Farmers Should Know",
      "> [!WARNING]\n> **Official Disbursement Advisory:**\n> While the cabinet has established the regulatory framework and budgetary approval, exact payment release dates are scheduled according to the provincial farming calendar. Farmers should beware of unauthorized agents demanding advance fees to release funds.",
      "## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)",
      "**Q1: What is the landholding cut-off for the cabinet subsidy?**\nThe ceiling is strictly set at **25 acres** of land.\n\n**Q2: Which bank processes the subsidy payments?**\nPayments are managed through **Sindh Bank** into Benazir Hari Card accounts.\n\n**Q3: Where can farmers report issues?**\nInquiries should be directed to the local Assistant Commissioner or District Agriculture Extension office.",
      "## Official Sources",
      "- [APP Sindh Cabinet Briefing](https://www.app.com.pk/sindh/sindh-cabinet-approves-wheat-support-package-edhi-medical-tower-digital-land-transfer-system/)\n- [Benazir Hari Card Portal](https://benazirharicard.gos.pk/)"
    ],
