    "content": [
      "# Sindh Job Portal 2026: Junior Clerk Vacancies Aur Online Application Ka Tarika",
      "> [!WARNING]\n> **Editorial Hold — Verification Notice:**\n> While the Government of Sindh has established the centralized **Sindh Job Portal (`sjp.gos.pk`)** to streamline provincial hiring, active recruitment schedules for Junior Clerk (BPS-11) positions are announced independently by individual government departments (such as Population Welfare, School Education, Labour, and Law).\n> \n> **Candidates are strongly advised to verify current department-specific advertisements and closing dates on the live portal before paying any testing or application fees.** This guide explains the official application workflow and standard statutory requirements.",
      "## Overview of the Sindh Job Portal (sjp.gos.pk)",
      "The Government of Sindh launched the **Sindh Job Portal** at [sjp.gos.pk](https://sjp.gos.pk/) to unify provincial recruitment across public departments. The platform allows job seekers residing in Sindh to create an official candidate profile, upload their educational credentials, and apply electronically for advertised positions.",
      "## Standard Eligibility Criteria for Junior Clerk (BPS-11)",
      "While specific advertisements govern each hiring cycle, provincial civil service rules for Junior Clerk (BPS-11) in Sindh typically require:\n\n1. **Academic Qualification:**\n   - Higher Secondary School Certificate (Intermediate, 12 years of education) in at least 2nd Division, OR\n   - Bachelor's Degree (Graduation) from an HEC-recognized university (preferred by several departments).\n2. **Computer Proficiency:**\n   - Mandatory minimum 6-month Certificate in **MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint)** from an institute recognized by the **Sindh Board of Technical Education (SBTE)** or Trade Testing Board (TTB).\n3. **Typing Speed:**\n   - Minimum typing speed of **30 words per minute (wpm)** on computer keyboard, tested during post-screening skill assessments.\n4. **Screening Test Qualification:**\n   - For departments utilizing third-party testing services (such as **Sukkur IBA Testing Service - STS**), candidates must meet the minimum passing threshold (typically 40% or 50% in the relevant category).\n5. **Domicile & Age Limit:**\n   - Must hold a valid Domicile and Permanent Resident Certificate (PRC / Form D) of Sindh.\n   - Age limit generally ranges from **18 to 28 years**, with standard upper age relaxation applicable under Sindh Government rules.",
      "## Step-by-Step Online Application Workflow on sjp.gos.pk",
      "When active positions are notified on the portal, follow these steps to submit your application:\n\n1. **Register on the Portal:** Visit [sjp.gos.pk](https://sjp.gos.pk/) and create a new account using your CNIC, email address, and mobile number.\n2. **Build Your Candidate Profile:**\n   - Enter personal details, domicile district (Urban/Rural), and mailing address.\n   - Add educational qualifications starting from Matriculation to highest degree.\n   - Upload technical certificates (MS Office diploma) and typing credentials.\n3. **Upload Mandatory Scanned Documents:**\n   - CNIC front and back.\n   - Domicile and PRC (Form D).\n   - Passport-sized photograph with blue/white background.\n   - Academic marksheets and certificates.\n4. **Browse Active Departmental Openings:** Go to the 'Jobs' section on the dashboard to locate open Junior Clerk listings.\n5. **Apply & Submit:** Confirm eligibility against the department's requirements, submit the application, and retain the generated application tracking ID.",
      "## Important Precaution Against Unofficial Advertisements",
      "> [!CAUTION]\n> **Avoid Fake Recruitment Agents:**\n> - The Sindh Government does not hire through private agents or unverified WhatsApp groups.\n> - Always cross-check vacancy notices published in daily newspapers against listings on `sjp.gos.pk` or the recruiting department's official website.\n> - Never hand over original educational certificates or unverified cash payments.",
      "## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)",
      "**Q1: What is the official website for Sindh Job Portal?**\nThe official address is [sjp.gos.pk](https://sjp.gos.pk/).\n\n**Q2: What is the basic pay scale for Junior Clerk in Sindh?**\nJunior Clerk is categorized under **Basic Pay Scale 11 (BPS-11)** in provincial government departments.\n\n**Q3: Is a computer certificate compulsory for Junior Clerk?**\nYes. A recognized certificate in MS Office (at least 6 months) from an SBTE/TTB recognized technical institute and a minimum 30 wpm typing speed are statutory requirements.\n\n**Q4: How do I know if a specific department's clerk jobs are currently open?**\nCheck the live vacancies tab directly on [sjp.gos.pk](https://sjp.gos.pk/) or monitor official departmental advertisements.",
      "## Official Sources & Related CareerDost Articles",
      "- **Official Sources:** [Government of Sindh](https://www.sindh.gov.pk/), [Sindh Job Portal](https://sjp.gos.pk/).\n- **Related Provincial Opportunities:** [SPSC Jobs 2026 - 54 Vacancies](https://careerdost.blog/jobs/spsc-jobs-2026-54-vacancies), [Sindh Courts Jobs 2026 BPS 1-4](https://careerdost.blog/jobs/sindh-courts-bps-1-4-jobs-2026)."
    ],
