    "lastDate": "2026-10-23",
    "noDeadline": false,
    "publishDate": "2026-10-12",
    "officialLink": "https://sindhhec.gov.pk/sindh-research-support-programme/",
    "applyLink": "https://sindhhec.gov.pk/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/APPLICATION-FORM-SRSP-2026-27-UPDATED-FINAL-1.pdf",
    "isVerified": true,
    "featured": true,
    "logoInitial": "SHEC",
    "featuredImage": "/images/sindh-hec-research-support-programme-2026-27.webp",
    "imageAlt": "Sindh HEC Research Support Programme 2026–27 research grants deadline 23 October",
    "excerpt": "Sindh HEC invites research proposals under SRSP 2026–27. Eligible public university faculty members in Sindh can seek grants of up to Rs5 million across physical, medical, engineering, and social sciences. Deadline: 23 October 2026.",
    "content": [
      "### Official Call for Research Proposals: Sindh HEC SRSP 2026–27",
      "The **Sindh Higher Education Commission (Sindh HEC)** has formally invited competitive research proposals from eligible faculty members under its flagship **Sindh Research Support Programme (SRSP) for the financial session 2026–27**.",
      "The programme is specifically designed to provide competitive project financing to address strategic scientific, educational, technological, socioeconomic, and environmental challenges facing Sindh.",
      "Eligible researchers may seek project funding of **up to Rs. 5 million (Rs. 5,000,000)** for a project duration of **two years**.",
      "> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Faculty Opportunity Only:** This programme is strictly intended for regular faculty members at Sindh's public sector universities and degree-awarding institutions. It is **not** an individual student scholarship for undergraduate or general BS students.",
      "### Programme Overview Summary",
      "- **Funding Agency:** Sindh Higher Education Commission (SHEC), Government of Sindh\n- **Programme Title:** Sindh Research Support Programme (SRSP) 2026–27\n- **Maximum Grant Amount:** Up to Rs. 5,000,000 per approved research project\n- **Project Duration:** Two (2) Years\n- **Application Deadline:** **23 October 2026**\n- **Target Beneficiaries:** Regular PhD and qualified clinical faculty of public-sector universities in Sindh\n- **Official Programme Notice:** [sindhhec.gov.pk/sindh-research-support-programme](https://sindhhec.gov.pk/sindh-research-support-programme/)\n- **Official Application Form:** [Download SRSP Application Form PDF](https://sindhhec.gov.pk/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/APPLICATION-FORM-SRSP-2026-27-UPDATED-FINAL-1.pdf)\n- **Official Advertisement:** [View SRSP 2026–27 Advertisement](https://sindhhec.gov.pk/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/SRSP-26-27.webp)",
      "### Eligible Thematic & Research Disciplines",
      "The official Sindh HEC circular covers a broad spectrum of research domains, with explicit funding allocations for:\n- **Natural & Physical Sciences:** Physics, Chemistry, Earth Sciences, Mathematics\n- **Medical & Health Sciences:** Clinical studies, epidemiology, diagnostics, pharmaceutical development\n- **Engineering & Emerging Technology:** Civil, electrical, mechanical, renewable energy systems\n- **Computing & Information Technology:** Artificial intelligence, data science, cybersecurity, software engineering\n- **Social Sciences & Management:** Economics, public policy, governance, education emergency strategies\n- **Agriculture, Food & Environmental Sciences:** Sustainable agriculture, water conservation, climate resilience",
      "> [!NOTE]\n> **Provincial Priority Areas:** In accordance with the official notice, preferential evaluation will be given to proposals directly addressing **Climate Change, Food Security, Water Management, Disaster Rehabilitation in Flood-affected areas, Public Health, Waterborne Diseases**, and initiatives with clear commercialization potential aligned with the UN Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).",
      "### Eligibility Criteria for Principal Investigators (PI)",
      "Applicants must meet all regulatory parameters specified in the official circular:\n1. Must be a regular, full-time faculty member at a public-sector university or chartered degree-awarding institution (DAI) located in Sindh.\n2. Must hold an earned PhD degree or recognized clinical terminal qualification (**FCPS, MCPS, FRCS** or equivalent).\n3. Must not currently be holding another active research grant from Sindh HEC as Principal Investigator.\n4. Faculty members who successfully received an SRSP award within the preceding two financial years are restricted from re-applying until completion.",
      "### Step-by-Step Submission Procedure",
      "1. Download the prescribed **SRSP 2026–27 Application Form** directly from the official Sindh HEC portal.\n2. Formulate your detailed project proposal including abstract, project background, methodology, work packages, equipment requirements, and itemized budgetary justification.\n3. Secure formal endorsement from your university's **Office of Research, Innovation & Commercialization (ORIC)** and head of institution (Vice Chancellor/Registrar).\n4. Assemble all mandatory supporting documentation including institutional endorsement certificate, CV of PI and Co-PI, and price quotations for major equipment.\n5. Submit the complete application dossier with the signed PDF in strict accordance with the official submission guidelines before **23 October 2026**.",
      "### Important Editorial Caveat",
      "The maximum grant of Rs5 million represents the upper funding ceiling per project, not an automatic grant disbursement. All submissions undergo technical peer review, ethical scrutiny, and competitive budgetary evaluation by the Sindh HEC Scientific Committee.",
      "### Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)",
      "**Q1: What is the last date to submit research proposals for Sindh HEC SRSP 2026–27?**\nThe official deadline is **23 October 2026**.\n\n**Q2: Can faculty members from private universities in Sindh apply?**\nNo. As per the official advertisement, SRSP 2026–27 is restricted to regular faculty members of public-sector universities and degree-awarding institutions in Sindh.\n\n**Q3: What is the maximum funding duration?**\nThe funding period is for up to two years.\n\n**Q4: Where can I obtain the official application form?**\nThe application form is available directly on the Sindh HEC portal: `sindhhec.gov.pk/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/APPLICATION-FORM-SRSP-2026-27-UPDATED-FINAL-1.pdf`."
    ],
