      "### Merit Scholarships & Tuition Fee Rebates",
      "UAJK maintains a structured tuition assistance program for high-achieving admitted students:\n- **Undergraduate Merit Rebate:** In each degree program, the top 3 semester merit-holders are awarded direct tuition fee rebates of **50% for 1st position**, **40% for 2nd position**, and **30% for 3rd position**.\n- **Need-Cum-Merit Support:** Low-income students meeting specified income thresholds may also apply through the Directorate of Students' Affairs (DSA) for partner welfare scholarships such as Muslim Hands Scholarships (MHS). *Note: These assistance schemes provide structured partial or merit rebates and should not be confused with unconditional full-ride funding.*",
