    "isVerified": true,
    "featured": true,
    "logoInitial": "NUST",
    "featuredImage": "/images/nust-net-2027-registration-series-1.webp",
    "imageAlt": "NUST NET 2027 Series 1 Registration Schedule & Apply Online CareerDost",
    "excerpt": "NUST NET 2027 Series 1 registration officially opens today, 4 October 2026. Submit your online application at ugadmissions.nust.edu.pk before 14 November 2026. Computer-based tests begin 17 November in Islamabad.",
    "content": [
      "### Executive Summary & Official Schedule Announcement",
      "Online registration for the **NUST Entry Test (NET) 2027 Series-1** officially commences today, **4 October 2026**, for admission into all undergraduate degree programmes at the **National University of Sciences and Technology (NUST)**. Students aspiring for undergraduate engineering, computing, business, applied sciences, and architecture programmes can register via the official NUST admissions portal (`ugadmissions.nust.edu.pk`).",
      "According to the official schedule published on NUST's *Dates to Remember* portal, the online application deadline for Series-1 is **14 November 2026**. The **Computer-Based NUST Entry Test (CBNET)** will commence from **17 November 2026 onwards** exclusively at the NUST Main Campus in Islamabad.",
      "### Quick Information Summary Table",
      "- **Conducting Authority:** National University of Sciences and Technology (NUST)\n- **Test Name:** NUST Entry Test (NET 2027 Series-1)\n- **Admission Intake:** Fall 2027 Undergraduate Admissions\n- **Online Registration Commences:** 4 October 2026 (Starts Today)\n- **Registration Deadline:** 14 November 2026\n- **CBNET Test Commencement:** 17 November 2026 onwards\n- **Series-1 Test Location:** NUST Main Campus, Sector H-12, Islamabad\n- **Test Format:** Computer-Based Test (CBNET) • 200 MCQs • 3 Hours • No Negative Marking\n- **Registration Fee:** Rs. 5,000 (Pakistani / Dual Nationals) • USD 80 / Rs. 10,000 (Foreign Nationals)\n- **Official Portal:** [ugadmissions.nust.edu.pk](https://ugadmissions.nust.edu.pk/)",
      "### Undergraduate Programmes Accepting NET 2027",
      "NUST Entry Test scores are accepted for admission across all premier schools and faculties of the university, including:\n1. **Engineering Disciplines:** Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Civil Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Aerospace & Avionics Engineering, Mechatronics, and Environmental Engineering.\n2. **Computing & AI Tracks:** Computer Science (CS), Software Engineering (SE), Artificial Intelligence (AI), Data Science, and Computer Engineering.\n3. **Business & Social Sciences:** Bachelor of Business Administration (BBA), BS Accounting & Finance, BS Economics, BS Psychology, and BS Public Administration.\n4. **Architecture & Design:** Bachelor of Architecture (B.Arch) and Bachelor of Industrial Design (BID).\n5. **Applied & Natural Sciences:** BS Biotechnology, BS Chemistry, BS Physics, and BS Mathematics.",
      "### Comprehensive Eligibility Criteria",
      "To be eligible for NET 2027 registration and subsequent NUST undergraduate admission, candidates must satisfy the following academic prerequisites:\n- **Minimum Academic Aggregate:** Candidates must have secured a minimum of **60% aggregate marks** in both SSC (Matriculation) and HSSC (Intermediate Part-1 / Complete) or equivalent examinations.\n- **O/A Level Candidates:** O/A Level candidates must possess an official equivalence certificate issued by the **Inter Boards Coordination Commission (IBCC)** with at least 60% marks in relevant science/mathematics subjects.\n- **Result Awaiting Students:** Students currently studying in HSSC Part-2 or A2 are fully eligible to apply on the basis of their Part-1 / O-Level results.",
      "### NET Test Structure & Subject Weightage",
      "The NUST Entry Test is a 3-hour computer-based exam consisting of 200 Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs). There is **strictly no negative marking** on any section of the test.\n\n- **Engineering & Computing Stream:** Mathematics (50% — 100 MCQs), Physics (30% — 60 MCQs), Chemistry / Computer Science (15% — 30 MCQs), and English (5% — 10 MCQs).\n- **Business & Social Sciences Stream:** Quantitative Mathematics (50% — 100 MCQs), English (40% — 80 MCQs), and Intelligence (10% — 20 MCQs).\n- **Applied Sciences & Biotechnology:** Biology (50% — 100 MCQs), Chemistry (30% — 60 MCQs), Physics (15% — 30 MCQs), and English (5% — 10 MCQs).\n- **Architecture & Industrial Design:** Design Aptitude (50% — 100 MCQs), Mathematics (30% — 60 MCQs), and English (20% — 40 MCQs).",
      "### Separate Registration Rule & Multiple Series Policy",
      "> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Crucial Rule on NET Series Attempts:** NUST conducts four distinct NET series (Series 1, 2, 3, and 4) throughout the academic year. A **separate online registration form and separate application fee** must be submitted for each individual series. Candidates are permitted to appear in multiple series; NUST's admission system automatically retains your **highest / best score** for final merit determination.",
      "### Official Merit Calculation Formula",
      "For undergraduate Engineering and Computing disciplines, the composite aggregate merit is calculated according to the officially confirmed formula:\n- **NUST Entry Test (NET):** 75% weightage\n- **HSSC / Intermediate Part-1 (or O-Level):** 15% weightage\n- **SSC / Matriculation:** 10% weightage",
      "### Step-by-Step Online Application Procedure",
      "1. **Visit Admission Portal:** Go to `https://ugadmissions.nust.edu.pk/`.\n2. **Account Registration:** Click on *New Registration*, enter your active email address, and verify your account credentials.\n3. **Profile & Academic Information:** Fill in your personal details, Matric/O-Level grades, and Intermediate college credentials.\n4. **Select Programme & Test Stream:** Choose your desired discipline stream (Engineering, Computing, Business, etc.).\n5. **Generate Fee Challan:** Download the computerized fee invoice of Rs. 5,000 and deposit it via 1Link, ATM, online banking, or designated commercial bank branches.\n6. **Schedule Test Slot:** Upon payment verification on the portal, select your preferred examination date and morning/afternoon session for CBNET in Islamabad before **14 November 2026**.",
      "### Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)",
      "**Q1: When does NUST NET 2027 Series-1 registration start and close?**\nRegistration opens today, **4 October 2026**, and closes on **14 November 2026**.\n\n**Q2: When will Series-1 tests be conducted?**\nComputer-based tests (CBNET) will commence from **17 November 2026 onwards**.\n\n**Q3: Where is the test centre for Series-1?**\nNET Series-1 is conducted exclusively as a computer-based test at the NUST Main Campus (Sector H-12), Islamabad.\n\n**Q4: Is there negative marking in NUST NET?**\nNo. There is no negative marking in any section of the NUST Entry Test.\n\n**Q5: Can I appear in more than one NET series?**\nYes. You can appear in multiple series. You must submit a separate form and fee for each series, and your best score will be counted for final merit.",
      "**Q6: What is the fee for NET 2027 Series-1?**\nThe application fee is Rs. 5,000 for Pakistani and dual-nationality candidates, and USD 80 (Rs. 10,000) for foreign nationals."
    ],
