    "id": 504,
    "slug": "szabist-ihsan-trust-interest-free-loan-2026-27",
    "title": "SZABIST Karachi Ihsan Trust Interest-Free Loan 2026–27: Qarz-e-Hasna Facility for University Students",
    "category": "scholarships",
    "organization": "SZABIST University Karachi & Ihsan Trust",
    "jobType": "Financial Assistance",
    "location": "SZABIST Karachi Campus",
    "qualification": "Enrolled Undergraduate or Graduate Students with Minimum CGPA 2.50",
    "salary": "100% Tuition Fee Coverage as Qarz-e-Hasna (Interest-Free Loan)",
    "experience": "Enrolled Students (Repayable in Monthly Installments Post-Graduation — NOT a Grant)",
    "positions": "Need-Based Financial Assistance Facility",
    "lastDate": "2026-11-16",
    "noDeadline": false,
    "publishDate": "2026-10-01",
    "officialLink": "https://szabist.edu.pk/announcements/",
    "applyLink": "https://portal.ihsantrust.org/",
    "isVerified": true,
    "featured": true,
    "logoInitial": "SZABIST",
    "featuredImage": "/images/szabist-ihsan-trust-interest-free-loan-2026.webp",
    "imageAlt": "SZABIST Karachi Ihsan Trust Interest-Free Loan Qarz-e-Hasna 2026-27",
    "excerpt": "SZABIST University Karachi, in partnership with Ihsan Trust, has announced the Interest-Free Loan Facility (Qarz-e-Hasna) for the 2026–27 academic year. Students with minimum 2.5 CGPA can apply online through portal.ihsantrust.org by 16 November 2026.",
    "content": [
      "### Educational Financing Overview: Ihsan Trust & SZABIST Partnership",
      "**SZABIST University Karachi**, in institutional collaboration with the **Ihsan Trust**, has officially opened applications for the **Ihsan Trust Interest-Free Loan Facility (Qarz-e-Hasna) for the Academic Year 2026–27**. Announced through SZABIST’s **External Relations and Financial Assistance (ERFA) Department**, this initiative is designed to ensure that no qualified student is forced to discontinue higher education due to temporary financial inability to pay semester tuition fees.",
      "The Ihsan Trust is Pakistan's premier Shariah-compliant educational endowment organization, providing pure **Qarz-e-Hasna** to deserving students across leading universities nationwide.",
      "**CRITICAL FINANCIAL DISCLOSURE:** This facility is strictly an **Interest-Free Loan (Qarz-e-Hasna)** and is **NOT a non-repayable grant, charity, or institutional scholarship**. Beneficiary students receive tuition assistance during their studies and commit to repaying the exact principal amount in affordable, interest-free monthly installments only after completing their degree and securing employment. Students seeking non-repayable grants should consult the [SZABIST Need-Based Scholarship (SNBSP) Guide](/jobs/szabist-scholarship-2026-27).",
      "### Quick Summary Table: SZABIST Ihsan Trust Qarz-e-Hasna 2026–27",
      "| Metric / Parameter | Official Facility Specification |\n|:---|:---|\n| **Facilitating Body** | Ihsan Trust in partnership with SZABIST University Karachi |\n| **Coordinating Department** | External Relations & Financial Assistance (ERFA), SZABIST |\n| **Facility Nature** | **100% Interest-Free Loan (Qarz-e-Hasna)** — Reimbursable post-graduation |\n| **Target Audience** | Enrolled Undergraduate & Graduate Students experiencing tuition distress |\n| **Academic Performance Requirement** | Minimum **2.50 CGPA** (or equivalent academic standing) |\n| **Program Exclusions** | **Media Sciences Degree Programs are strictly excluded** |\n| **Application Portal** | [portal.ihsantrust.org](https://portal.ihsantrust.org/) |\n| **Announcement Date** | 01 October 2026 |\n| **Final Application Deadline** | **16 November 2026** |\n| **Helpdesk Contact** | erfa@szabist.edu.pk |",
      "### Eligibility Benchmark & Strict Exclusions",
      "To qualify for consideration by the joint SZABIST–Ihsan Trust Financial Assistance Committee, applicants must fulfill all institutional conditions:",
      "1. **Enrolment Status:** Must be a currently registered, active student in an approved undergraduate or graduate degree program at SZABIST University Karachi.\n2. **Academic Standing:** Must maintain a cumulative grade point average of at least **2.50 CGPA** on a 4.0 scale.\n3. **Demonstrated Financial Need:** The applicant’s family must demonstrate genuine financial distress, evidenced through authentic utility bills, salary slips, or pension records.\n4. **Excluded Disciplines:** Per specific endowment terms, students enrolled in **Department of Media Sciences programs (such as BS Media Studies or MS Media Studies) are NOT eligible** for this facility.\n5. **Repayment Commitment:** The candidate and their guardian must execute a formal agreement committing to repay the interest-free principal balance in nominal monthly installments once gainfully employed post-graduation.",
      "### Step-by-Step Online Application Procedure via Ihsan Trust Portal",
      "Applications for the 2026–27 academic cycle are processed exclusively online through the dedicated Ihsan Trust system:",
      "1. **Navigate to the Portal:** Access the official application engine at [https://portal.ihsantrust.org/](https://portal.ihsantrust.org/).\n2. **New Applicants (First-Time Registration):**\n   - Click on **Register / Sign Up**.\n   - Complete your student profile using your authentic CNIC number, SZABIST student registration ID, active email address, and mobile number.\n   - Fill out the detailed family income, expense, and tuition fee breakdown.\n   - Upload mandatory scanned documents (CNIC of student & parents, recent utility bills, rent agreement if applicable, fee challan, and latest official transcript).\n3. **Existing Beneficiaries (Renewal / Re-application Cases):**\n   - Students who previously availed Ihsan Trust assistance must log in using their previously registered email address.\n   - Use your registered CNIC number (without dashes) as your default password.\n   - Update your current CGPA, upload your latest semester fee voucher and grade sheet, and submit for renewal.\n4. **Institutional Review:** After online submission, the SZABIST ERFA Department verifies institutional enrolment and schedules an evaluation interview before forwarding shortlisted files to Ihsan Trust Trustees for final approval.\n5. **Application Cut-Off Date:** The portal will close on **16 November 2026**.",
      "### Transparency & Anti-Fraud Advisory",
      "CareerDost urges all applicants to heed the following precautions:\n- **Direct Application:** Never use unauthorized third-party agents or social media brokers claiming to guarantee Ihsan Trust approvals. The application process on `portal.ihsantrust.org` is completely free.\n- **No Commission:** Ihsan Trust and SZABIST never solicit fees, commissions, or processing deposits.\n- **Official Helpdesk:** For legitimate guidance on application forms, reach out to the SZABIST ERFA desk in Karachi via `erfa@szabist.edu.pk` or review institutional policies on the [CareerDost Editorial Desk](/about#editorial-policy).",
      "### Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)",
      "**Q1: Is the Ihsan Trust facility at SZABIST a scholarship or a loan?**  \nIt is strictly an interest-free loan (Qarz-e-Hasna). Beneficiary students are required to repay the exact principal amount in flexible monthly installments after graduation and employment.\n\n**Q2: Are Media Sciences students eligible to apply?**  \nNo. The Ihsan Trust policy specifically excludes students enrolled in Media Sciences programs from this funding scheme.\n\n**Q3: What is the minimum CGPA required?**  \nApplicants must maintain a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.50 to qualify for loan consideration."
    ],
    "seoTitle": "SZABIST Ihsan Trust Interest-Free Loan 2026–27 (Qarz-e-Hasna) — Apply",
    "metaDescription": "SZABIST University Karachi announces Ihsan Trust Interest-Free Loan (Qarz-e-Hasna) for 2026–27. Minimum 2.5 CGPA required. Apply online via portal.ihsantrust.org by 16 Nov 2026.",
    "focusKeyword": "SZABIST Ihsan Trust Interest-Free Loan 2026-27",
    "status": "published",
    "createdAt": "2026-10-19 05:37:10",
    "updatedAt": "2026-10-19 06:16:29"
