    "slug": "hec-peridot-research-program-phase-13-2026",
    "title": "HEC PERIDOT Research Program Phase XIII: Franco-Pakistani Grant Guide",
    "category": "scholarships",
    "organization": "Higher Education Commission (HEC) / Campus France",
    "jobType": "Joint Franco-Pakistani Research Grant",
    "location": "Pakistan & France University Mobility",
    "qualification": "University Faculty & PhD Researchers",
    "salary": "Joint Research Funding & Academic Travel Stipend",
    "experience": "",
    "positions": "",
    "lastDate": "2026-09-30",
    "noDeadline": false,
    "publishDate": "2026-09-29",
    "officialLink": "https://www.hec.gov.pk/english/services/faculty/peridot/pages/default.aspx",
    "applyLink": "https://research.hec.gov.pk/",
    "isVerified": true,
    "featured": true,
    "logoInitial": "HEC",
    "featuredImage": "/images/hec-peridot-research-2026.webp",
    "imageAlt": "HEC PERIDOT Research Program 2026 Phase XIII Bilateral Grants CareerDost",
    "excerpt": "Proposal Call Closed (30 September 2026): Reference guide for HEC Pakistan and Campus France PERIDOT Research Program Phase XIII (Hubert Curien Partnership), covering joint review stages, priority themes, and mobility grant rules.",
    "content": [
      "> [!NOTE]\n> **Grant Call Status — Phase XIII Proposal Submission Closed:**\n> - **Sponsoring Agencies:** Higher Education Commission (**HEC**) Pakistan & Ministries of Europe/Foreign Affairs and Higher Education & Research, France (via **Campus France**).\n> - **Program:** PERIDOT Research Program — **Phase XIII** (Partenariat Hubert Curien — PHC).\n> - **Call Closing Date:** Joint online submissions closed on **30 September 2026 (16:00 PST)**.\n> - **Current Stage:** Bilateral eligibility screening, independent scientific peer review in Pakistan and France, and joint selection committee evaluation.\n> - **Official HEC Portal:** [HEC PERIDOT Official Page](https://www.hec.gov.pk/english/services/faculty/peridot/pages/default.aspx) | [HEC Research Portal (research.hec.gov.pk)](https://research.hec.gov.pk/).",
      "The **PERIDOT Research Program (Phase XIII)** is Pakistan's flagship bilateral Franco-Pakistani academic mobility initiative, jointly implemented by the **Higher Education Commission (HEC)** and **Campus France**. Designed to foster new research partnerships between Pakistani public/private HEC-recognized universities and French higher education or research laboratories, the Phase XIII proposal window closed on **30 September 2026** and is now in the bilateral scientific evaluation phase.",
      "## Phase XIII Grant Scope, Thematic Areas & Mobility Coverage",
      "| Grant Parameter | Official PERIDOT Bilateral Specification |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Pakistani Executing Body** | Research & Development Division, Higher Education Commission (HEC) |\n| **French Executing Body** | Ministry for Europe & Foreign Affairs (MEAE), MESR & Campus France |\n| **Eligible Principal Investigators** | Full-time PhD faculty members at HEC-recognized Pakistani universities paired with a French Principal Investigator |\n| **Priority Thematic Domains** | Health & Biomedical Sciences, Climate Change & Environmental Economics, Renewable Energy, and Sustainable Agriculture |\n| **Project Duration** | Up to **3 Years** (subject to annual progress and financial utilization review) |\n| **What Funding Covers** | International return airfare, visa/insurance support, and per-diem living allowances for short-term researcher & PhD student exchange |",
      "## Mandatory Dual-Submission & ORIC Compliance Rules",
      "Faculty teams tracking their Phase XIII dossiers—or preparing early for Phase XIV—should note the strict bilateral eligibility rules enforced by HEC and Campus France:\n- **Simultaneous Identical Submission:** A proposal is valid **only** if the Pakistani Principal Investigator (PI) submitted via [research.hec.gov.pk](https://research.hec.gov.pk/) **and** the partner French PI simultaneously submitted the matching proposal on the **Campus France PHC** portal before the deadline.\n- **ORIC Institutional Endorsement:** Pakistani university applications require formal endorsement from the university's **Office of Research, Innovation and Commercialization (ORIC)** and Vice Chancellor/Rector sign-off confirming workload allocation and existing laboratory infrastructure.\n- **Active Grant Cap & PhD Student Participation:** PERIDOT strongly prioritizes projects that train enrolled Pakistani and French **PhD scholars** through reciprocal laboratory stays, while PIs holding delinquent HEC research grants face administrative screening holds.",
      "## Bilateral Evaluation Timeline & Active Research Alternatives",
      "Following the **30 September 2026** cutoff, both sides independently grade scientific merit, methodological novelty, and complementarity of the two labs before convening the Joint Franco-Pakistani Selection Committee.\n- **Track Your Proposal:** Pakistani PIs can monitor review status inside their faculty account on [research.hec.gov.pk](https://research.hec.gov.pk/).\n- **Related Research & Mobility Funding:** Faculty and doctoral scholars can also explore our guides on the [Sindh HEC Research Support Programme 2026–27](/jobs/sindh-hec-research-support-programme-2026-27), [HEC IRSIP Batch 60 PhD Mobility Scholarship](/jobs/hec-irsip-batch-60-scholarship-2026), and [HEC Outstanding Research Awards](/jobs/hec-outstanding-research-awards-2026-27).",
      "## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)",
      "### Does PERIDOT fund heavy laboratory equipment purchases or full salaries?\nNo. As a Hubert Curien Partnership (PHC) mobility grant, PERIDOT primarily funds researcher and doctoral scholar **international travel and subsistence allowances** between Pakistan and France (with modest operational consumables on the Pakistani side per HEC budget ceilings), assuming baseline lab facilities already exist at both host institutions.",
      "### Where can Pakistani scholars find currently open international grants and scholarships?\nWhile PERIDOT Phase XIII closed on **30 September 2026**, you can check active postgraduate fellowships and bilateral scholarships in [Scholarships in Pakistan](/category/scholarships)."
    ],
    "seoTitle": "HEC PERIDOT Research Program Phase XIII — Grant Guide",
