    "excerpt": "Admissions Closed (29 September 2026): Reference guide for University of Haripur (UOH) Fall 2026 BS 4-Year, BS 5th-Semester bridge, Medical Lab Technology (MLT), and Diploma programs, covering merit scrutiny and spring intake monitoring.",
    "content": [
      "> [!NOTE]\n> **Admission Cycle Status — Fall 2026 Registrations Closed:**\n> - **University:** The University of Haripur (**UOH**), Hattar Road, Haripur, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa.\n> - **Programs Covered:** BS (4-Year), BS 5th-Semester (Lateral Entry), Medical Lab Technology (MLT), and Undergraduate Diplomas.\n> - **Final Application Deadline:** Closed on **29 September 2026**.\n> - **Current Stage:** Departmental merit list conclusion, original document verification, and preparation for upcoming Spring admission notifications on [uoh.edu.pk](https://www.uoh.edu.pk/admissions/schedule).",
      "The **University of Haripur (UOH)**—a public-sector HEC-recognized university serving Hazara Division and Khyber Pakhtunkhwa—concluded online applications for its **Fall 2026 undergraduate, lateral-entry, and diploma intake** on **29 September 2026**. Students who secured provisional placement during Fall merit rounds or who are preparing academic credentials for UOH's next semester cycle can use this verified guide to review eligibility benchmarks and document scrutiny rules.",
      "## Fall 2026 Academic Tracks & Minimum Eligibility Standards",
      "| Program Category | Representative UOH Departments | Standard Eligibility Criteria |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **BS (4-Year Undergraduate)** | Computer Science, Software Engineering, AI, Information Security, Psychology, Forestry, Environmental Sciences, Management Sciences, Economics | HSSC (F.Sc / ICS / FA / I.Com) or DAE / IBCC equivalent with minimum **45%–50% marks** (50% required for Computing & Allied Health disciplines per NCEAC/council norms) |\n| **BS Medical Lab Technology (MLT) & Public Health** | Allied Health & Biological Sciences | F.Sc Pre-Medical (or relevant MLT equivalence) with minimum **50% marks** |\n| **BS 5th-Semester (Bridge / Lateral Entry)** | Selected Arts, Social, Computing & Management Sciences | 14-Year **ADP / Associate Degree** (or conventional BA/BSc) from an HEC-recognized university with minimum 2.00 CGPA / 45% marks in relevant subject |\n| **Specialized Diplomas** | One-Year / Undergraduate Skill & Allied Diplomas | HSSC or Matric/Bachelor qualification as specified per departmental notice |",
      "## Merit Calculation, Quota Allocation & Fee Confirmation Rules",
      "Admissions at the University of Haripur follow transparent public-sector merit regulations approved by the UOH Academic Council:\n- **Open Merit & Reserved Seats:** Alongside open merit seats, UOH allocates statutory quotas for KP districts/merged areas, sports, Hafiz-e-Quran (subject to oral test), persons with disabilities, and overseas Pakistanis.\n- **5th-Semester Credit Evaluation:** Departmental Equivalence Committees inspect ADP/Associate Degree transcripts to determine whether bridging deficiency courses are required before 5th-semester placement.\n- **Fee Voucher Validity:** Provisionally selected students must deposit bank fee vouchers within the deadline printed on each merit list at [uoh.edu.pk/admissions/schedule](https://www.uoh.edu.pk/admissions/schedule); unclaimed seats pass to subsequent waiting lists.",
      "## Document Checklist for Campus Enrollment Scrutiny",
      "Enrolling candidates at UOH Haripur must submit attested copies and show originals at their respective teaching department (check full attestation and equivalence steps in our [Academic & Official Documents Checklist 2026](/jobs/government-jobs-documents-checklist-pakistan-2026)):\n- Printed UOH online application form and paid bank fee challan.\n- Original **SSC (Matric)** and **HSSC (Intermediate)** DMCs and BISE certificates (plus 14-year ADP transcript for BS 5th-Semester entrants).\n- **Character Certificate** from the last attended college/institution and **Migration Certificate** where required.\n- Student **NADRA CNIC / Form-B**, Father/Guardian CNIC, **Domicile Certificate**, and passport-size photographs.",
      "## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)",
      "### Can new students still submit Fall 2026 forms at the University of Haripur?\nNo. The Fall 2026 online admission portal closed on **29 September 2026**. Prospective students should monitor [uoh.edu.pk/admissions/schedule](https://www.uoh.edu.pk/admissions/schedule) for Spring admissions or check active intakes in [University Admissions in Pakistan](/category/admissions).",
      "### What test is required if I plan to apply for UOH MS/MPhil programs next semester?\nPostgraduate MS/MPhil applicants in KP public universities generally require a valid GAT General or institutional test—see our [NTS GAT General Registration & Schedule Guide](/jobs/nts-gat-general-viii-2026-registration-schedule-eligibility) and [University of Malakand Admissions Guide](/jobs/university-of-malakand-admissions-2026) for comparable public university benchmarks."
    ],
