    "id": 81,
    "slug": "sbbu-fully-funded-scholarship-2026",
    "title": "SBBU Shaheed Benazirabad Scholarship 2026: SFAO Financial Aid & Fee Waiver Guide",
    "category": "scholarships",
    "organization": "Shaheed Benazir Bhutto University (SBBU), Shaheed Benazirabad",
    "jobType": "100% Tuition Fee Waiver Scholarship",
    "location": "Shaheed Benazirabad (Nawabshah), Sanghar & Naushahro Feroze, Sindh",
    "qualification": "Enrolled / Admitted Students (BS, BBA, MS, MPhil, PhD)",
    "salary": "100% Full Tuition Waiver + Financial Support",
    "experience": "",
    "positions": "",
    "lastDate": "2026-09-29",
    "noDeadline": false,
    "publishDate": "2026-09-28",
    "officialLink": "https://sbbusba.edu.pk/sbbu-main/financial-aid-office.html",
    "applyLink": "https://admissions.sbbusba.edu.pk/",
    "isVerified": true,
    "featured": true,
    "logoInitial": "SBBU",
    "featuredImage": "/images/sbbu-scholarship-2026.webp",
    "imageAlt": "CareerDost.blog editorial banner for SBBU Shaheed Benazirabad SFAO scholarship and financial aid guide",
    "excerpt": "Applications Closed (29 September 2026): Official Students Financial Aid Office (SFAO) reference guide for Shaheed Benazir Bhutto University (SBBU), Shaheed Benazirabad (Nawabshah, Sanghar & Naushahro Feroze campuses), covering Merit-Cum-Need, Zakat, Bait-ul-Mal, and SEEF tuition assistance.",
    "content": [
      "> [!NOTE]\n> **Scholarship Cycle Notice — Session 2026–27 Window Closed:**\n> - **Institution:** Shaheed Benazir Bhutto University (**SBBU**), Shaheed Benazirabad (Nawabshah), Sindh.\n> - **Campuses Covered:** Main Campus Shaheed Benazirabad (Civil Lines, Nawabshah), Sanghar Campus, and Naushahro Feroze Campus.\n> - **Admission-Linked Scholarship Deadline:** Closed on **29 September 2026** alongside Batch 2027 admission registrations.\n> - **Official SFAO Source:** [SBBU Students Financial Aid Office (sbbusba.edu.pk)](https://sbbusba.edu.pk/sbbu-main/financial-aid-office.html) | [Admissions Portal](https://admissions.sbbusba.edu.pk/).",
      "**Shaheed Benazir Bhutto University (SBBU), Shaheed Benazirabad** facilitates tuition relief and subsistence grants for deserving undergraduate and postgraduate students across Sindh through its dedicated **Students Financial Aid Office (SFAO)**. While the admission-linked registration window for Academic Session 2026–27 closed on **29 September 2026**, newly enrolled students who secured seats via the [SBBU Undergraduate Merit List 2027](/jobs/sbbu-merit-list-2027) or [SBBU MS, MPhil & MBA Merit List 2027](/jobs/sbbu-ms-mphil-mba-merit-list-2027) should understand how SFAO processes departmental financial aid and external donor calls during the academic year.",
      "## Official SFAO Financial Aid & Scholarship Streams at SBBU SBA",
      "| Scholarship / Aid Scheme | Sponsoring Body | Target Beneficiaries & Coverage |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **SBBU Merit-Cum-Need Scholarship** | SBBU Shaheed Benazirabad Internal Fund | Enrolled BS, BBA, LLB, MS/MPhil & PhD students demonstrating strong GPA/merit and verified household financial need |\n| **HEC Need-Based Scholarships** | Higher Education Commission (HEC) via SFAO | Deserving undergraduate students covering semester tuition waivers and notified stipends per HEC rules |\n| **Sindh Educational Endowment Fund (SEEF)** | Government of Sindh | Sindh-domiciled students meeting provincial merit and family income thresholds |\n| **Pakistan Bait-ul-Mal (PBM) & Zakat Aid** | Federal PBM / District Zakat & Ushr Committee | Eligible *Mustahiq* students submitting a verified Zakat **Istehqaq Certificate** or PBM scrutiny file |",
      "## SFAO Institutional Scrutiny & Committee Interview Process",
      "Under SBBU Shaheed Benazirabad's financial aid framework, scholarships are awarded only after multi-step documentary verification—never on unverified verbal claims:\n1. **Departmental Verification:** Enrolled students submit the prescribed SFAO Financial Aid Form once their admission and semester enrollment are confirmed at Main Campus (Nawabshah), Sanghar, or Naushahro Feroze.\n2. **Household Income & Asset Audit:** The Institutional Scholarship Award Committee (ISAC) reviews guardian income proofs, utility expenses, family size, and dependent educational outlays.\n3. **SFAO Contact & Guidance:** Students can verify active donor calls directly at the **Students Financial Aid Office**, SBBU Main Campus, Civil Lines, Shaheed Benazirabad (Director SFAO: Mr. Noshad Ahmed Shaikh — official portal: [sbbusba.edu.pk/sbbu-main/financial-aid-office.html](https://sbbusba.edu.pk/sbbu-main/financial-aid-office.html)).",
      "## Mandatory Supporting Documents for SFAO Applications",
      "Keep attested copies of the following documents ready when SFAO announces semester-wise donor intakes (organize your academic and identity records with our [Government & Academic Documents Checklist 2026](/jobs/government-jobs-documents-checklist-pakistan-2026)):\n- Student NADRA CNIC (or Form-B) and Father/Guardian CNIC copies (or death certificate in case of orphan applicants).\n- Sindh **Domicile Certificate** and **PRC (Form-D)**.\n- Matric, Intermediate, and latest SBBU semester transcript / admission fee paid challan.\n- **Guardian Income Proof:** Official salary slip/pension book for salaried parents, or verifiable income certificate/tax return for self-employed or agricultural households.\n- Last three months' **electricity, gas, and water bills**, house rent agreement (if living in rented accommodation), and original **Istehqaq Certificate** from the District Zakat Office (strictly for Zakat-funded waivers).",
      "## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)",
      "### Does this scholarship apply to SBBU Shaheed Benazirabad in Sindh?\nYes. This guide exclusively covers **Shaheed Benazir Bhutto University, Shaheed Benazirabad (Sindh)** ([sbbusba.edu.pk](https://sbbusba.edu.pk/sbbu-main/financial-aid-office.html)) and its sub-campuses in Sanghar and Naushahro Feroze. Students should always verify the university name and province carefully before applying.",
      "### Can newly admitted Batch 2027 students still apply for external scholarships?\nWhile the **29 September 2026** initial admission cycle has closed (see our [SBBU Admissions 2026–27 Reference Guide](/jobs/sbbu-admissions-2026-deadline-extended)), enrolled SBBU students can apply whenever SFAO opens semester calls for SEEF, HEC Need-Based, Bait-ul-Mal, or Zakat scholarships. Browse currently open national funding programs in [Scholarships in Pakistan](/category/scholarships)."
    ],
