    "title": "NAVTTC Director (BPS-18) Jobs 2026: 10 Management Vacancies Guide via NJP",
    "category": "government-jobs",
    "organization": "National Vocational & Technical Training Commission (NAVTTC)",
    "jobType": "Government (BPS-18)",
    "location": "Islamabad / Regional Headquarters",
    "qualification": "Master's Degree (16-18 Years Education) in Public Administration, Management, Engineering, or Social Sciences",
    "salary": "BPS-18 Federal Government Pay Scale & Executive Allowances",
    "experience": "Minimum 5 Years Post-Qualification Managerial / Administrative / TVET Experience",
    "positions": "10 Senior Management Posts — Director (BPS-18)",
    "lastDate": "2026-10-10",
    "noDeadline": false,
    "publishDate": "2026-09-27",
    "officialLink": "https://navttc.gov.pk/",
    "applyLink": "https://www.njp.gov.pk/",
    "isVerified": false,
    "featured": true,
    "logoInitial": "NAV",
    "featuredImage": "/images/navttc-director-bps18-2026.webp",
    "imageAlt": "NAVTTC Jobs 2026 Director BPS 18 Vacancies Skills & TVET CareerDost",
    "excerpt": "Applications Closed (10 October 2026): Reference and scrutiny guide for 10 senior Director (BPS-18) positions at NAVTTC via NJP, detailing 5-year post-qualification experience verification, Departmental NOC rules, and selection board stages.",
    "content": [
      "> [!NOTE]\n> **Recruitment Status Notice — Applications Closed:**\n> - **Hiring Commission:** National Vocational & Technical Training Commission ([NAVTTC](https://navttc.gov.pk/)), Islamabad.\n> - **Cadre:** Director (**BPS-18**) — **10 Senior Management Posts**.\n> - **Closing Date:** Online submissions closed on **10 October 2026**.\n> - **Current Stage:** Scrutiny of 5-year post-qualification experience dossiers and Departmental Selection Board (DSB) shortlisting via [njp.gov.pk](https://www.njp.gov.pk/).",
      "As part of its October 2026 institutional strengthening drive (published alongside [BPS-15 Assistant](/jobs/navttc-assistant-bps15-jobs-2026) and [BPS-16 APS](/jobs/navttc-assistant-private-secretary-jobs-2026) posts), **NAVTTC** invited applications for **10 senior positions of Director (BPS-18)**. While the application deadline passed on **10 October 2026**, senior public- and private-sector applicants now face rigorous documentary scrutiny of their academic and managerial credentials.",
      "## BPS-18 Qualification & Experience Matrix",
      "| Parameter | Official BPS-18 Recruitment Standard |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Employer** | National Vocational & Technical Training Commission (NAVTTC) |\n| **Post & Pay Scale** | Director (**BPS-18**, Executive Federal Cadre) — **10 Vacancies** |\n| **Academic Requirement** | Second Class or Grade 'C' Master's / 16–18 Year Degree in Public Administration, MBA, Engineering, Education, Economics, or Social Sciences (HEC-recognized) |\n| **Mandatory Experience** | Minimum **5 years post-qualification** administrative, policy, project management, or TVET planning experience in government, autonomous, or reputable corporate bodies |\n| **Age Limit** | 25–35 years plus 5 years general federal relaxation (**up to 40 years**; additional service relaxation for eligible civil servants per rules) |",
      "## Executive Scrutiny Rules for BPS-18 Applicants",
      "For BPS-18 appointments, scrutiny committees evaluate experience and regulatory compliance far more strictly than entry-level clerical posts:\n- **Post-Qualification Tenure Calculation:** Only full-time managerial or executive experience accrued *after* the declaration date of the qualifying 16-year/Master's degree counts toward the 5-year threshold. Review Mistake #5 in our [NJP Application Rejection: 12 Common Mistakes Guide](/jobs/njp-application-rejection-12-common-mistakes-avoid).\n- **Verifiable Service Certificates:** Offer letters or pay slips alone are insufficient at interview stage; candidates must hold signed service/experience certificates on official letterhead stating exact `DD-MM-YYYY` dates and executive job responsibilities.\n- **Departmental NOC (In-Service Officers):** Officers currently serving in federal ministries, provincial departments, universities, or autonomous bodies must produce an official **No Objection Certificate (NOC)** / Through-Proper-Channel permission at the time of interview.",
      "## Portfolio Scope & Interview Preparation",
      "Shortlisted candidates appearing before the Departmental Selection Board should prepare across NAVTTC's statutory mandate under the NAVTTC Act:\n- **National Skills Strategy & Competency-Based Training (CBT&A):** Alignment of Pakistani TVET qualifications with the National Vocational Qualifications Framework (NVQF).\n- **International Skill Mobility:** Mutual recognition of technical certifications with GCC, European, and East Asian labor markets.\n- **Public Finance & PPRA Compliance:** PSDP project execution, public procurement rules (PPRA), and audit compliance.\n- Verify your complete interview folder early with our [Government Jobs Documents Checklist 2026](/jobs/government-jobs-documents-checklist-pakistan-2026) and [Job Application Readiness Checker](/tools/job-readiness-checker).",
      "## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)",
      "### How will shortlisted BPS-18 candidates be notified?\nShortlisting updates, test/assessment notices (if conducted), and interview call letters are communicated through the candidate dashboard on [njp.gov.pk](https://www.njp.gov.pk/) and official announcements on [navttc.gov.pk](https://navttc.gov.pk/).",
      "### Where can experienced professionals find open BPS-17 to BPS-19 federal jobs?\nCheck active senior public-sector listings in [Government Jobs in Pakistan](/category/government-jobs) and monthly consolidated gazetted recruitments covered in our [FPSC Online Application Guide](/jobs/fpsc-online-application-challan-form-32a-guide)."
    ],
