    "salary": "BPS-16 Federal Government Pay Scale",
    "experience": "Secretarial Shorthand (100 WPM), Computer Typing (50 WPM) & MS Office Proficiency",
    "positions": "11 Regular Posts — Assistant Private Secretary (BPS-16)",
    "lastDate": "2026-10-10",
    "noDeadline": false,
    "publishDate": "2026-09-27",
    "officialLink": "https://navttc.gov.pk/",
    "applyLink": "https://www.njp.gov.pk/",
    "isVerified": false,
    "featured": true,
    "logoInitial": "NAV",
    "featuredImage": "/images/navttc-assistant-private-secretary-2026.webp",
    "imageAlt": "NAVTTC Assistant Private Secretary Jobs 2026 – Apply Online — National Vocational & Technical Training Commission (NAVTTC) Official Notice CareerDost",
    "excerpt": "Applications Closed (10 October 2026): Complete post-application test and scrutiny guide for 11 NAVTTC Assistant Private Secretary (BPS-16) posts, covering 100 WPM shorthand dictation, 50 WPM typing benchmarks, and NJP status tracking.",
    "content": [
      "> [!NOTE]\n> **Recruitment Status Notice — Applications Closed:**\n> - **Hiring Commission:** National Vocational & Technical Training Commission ([NAVTTC](https://navttc.gov.pk/)).\n> - **Designation:** Assistant Private Secretary (APS, **BPS-16**) — **11 Regular Vacancies**.\n> - **Closing Date:** Online applications closed on **10 October 2026**.\n> - **Current Stage:** Scrutiny of applications and scheduling of practical English shorthand & typing tests via [njp.gov.pk](https://www.njp.gov.pk/).",
      "NAVTTC invited applications from secretarial professionals across Pakistan for **11 regular BPS-16 posts of Assistant Private Secretary (APS)** alongside its [BPS-15 Assistant](/jobs/navttc-assistant-bps15-jobs-2026) and [BPS-18 Director](/jobs/navttc-director-bps18-jobs-2026) recruitment drive. With registrations closed on **10 October 2026**, eligible applicants should focus on practical shorthand transcription accuracy and computer typing speed ahead of skill testing.",
      "## Verified BPS-16 Eligibility & Skill Benchmarks",
      "| Parameter | Prescribed Federal APS (BPS-16) Standard |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Commission** | National Vocational & Technical Training Commission (NAVTTC), Islamabad |\n| **Total Vacancies** | **11 Posts** (Merit & Provincial/Regional Quotas) |\n| **Academic Qualification** | Second Class or Grade 'C' Bachelor's Degree (14 or 16 years) from an HEC-recognized university |\n| **English Shorthand Speed** | Minimum **100 Words Per Minute (WPM)** |\n| **Computer Typing Speed** | Minimum **50 Words Per Minute (WPM)** on PC keyboard |\n| **Computer Literacy** | Practical command of MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint, diary management & official drafting |\n| **Age Limit** | 20–28 years plus 5 years general federal age relaxation (**up to 33 years**) |",
      "## How Federal APS Shorthand & Typing Skill Tests Work",
      "Unlike purely MCQ-based clerical posts, BPS-16 APS selection hinges on practical skill elimination stages:\n1. **Computer Typing Speed Test (50 WPM):** Timed passage typing on PC where net speed is calculated after deducting spelling, spacing, and punctuation errors. Practice clean accuracy above 55 gross WPM to stay safely clear of the 50 WPM cutoff.\n2. **English Shorthand Dictation (100 WPM):** A timed dictation passage (typically 4–5 minutes at 100 WPM) recorded in Pitman/Gregg shorthand notes, followed by a fixed computer transcription window where both shorthand outlines and transcribed text are submitted.\n3. **Office Noting & Viva Voce:** Shortlisted qualifiers appear before the selection committee to demonstrate executive calendar handling, confidential file movement, and Secretariat Instructions familiarity.",
      "## NJP Status Verification & Required Documents",
      "Check your **Applied Jobs** dashboard on [https://www.njp.gov.pk](https://www.njp.gov.pk) and official notices on [navttc.gov.pk](https://navttc.gov.pk/) for skill-test roll-number slips.\n- **Check Skill Entries & Scrutiny Rules:** As highlighted in our [NJP Application Rejection: 12 Common Mistakes Guide](/jobs/njp-application-rejection-12-common-mistakes-avoid), omitting typing/shorthand speeds in your NJP profile or holding a post-deadline domicile can affect shortlisting.\n- **Document Dossier:** Organize original and attested copies of your CNIC, Domicile, Bachelor's degree/transcript, shorthand/typing institute certificates, and NOC (if in government service) using our [Government Jobs Documents Checklist 2026](/jobs/government-jobs-documents-checklist-pakistan-2026) and [Job Readiness Checker](/tools/job-readiness-checker).",
      "## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)",
      "### What is the difference between BPS-14 Stenotypist and BPS-16 APS speed requirements?\nFederal Stenotypist (BPS-14) vacancies—such as [Cabinet Division Stenotypist Jobs](/jobs/cabinet-division-stenotypist-jobs-bps-14-2026)—typically require **80 WPM shorthand and 40 WPM typing** with Intermediate qualification, whereas BPS-16 Assistant Private Secretary requires a **Bachelor's degree plus 100 WPM shorthand and 50 WPM typing**.",
      "### Can I still apply for NAVTTC APS (BPS-16) posts?\nNo, the online window closed on **10 October 2026**. Visit [Government Jobs in Pakistan](/category/government-jobs) or review our [FPSC Online Application & Challan 32-A Guide](/jobs/fpsc-online-application-challan-form-32a-guide) for upcoming federal BPS-16 APS consolidated advertisements."
    ],
