    "excerpt": "Applications Closed (01 October 2026): Reference guide for TIMES University Multan (TUM) Lecturer and Assistant Professor recruitment across Law, Microbiology, Biochemistry, Economics, and Management Sciences.",
    "content": [
      "> [!NOTE]\n> **Recruitment Status Notice — Applications Closed:**\n> - **Hiring Institution:** TIMES University, Multan (**TUM**), Southern Punjab (HEC-recognized chartered university).\n> - **Advertised Roles:** Assistant Professor & Lecturer.\n> - **Departments Covered:** Law, Microbiology, Biochemistry, Economics, and Management Sciences.\n> - **Closing Date:** Applications closed on **01 October 2026**.\n> - **Official Careers Page:** [tum.edu.pk/jobs/](https://www.tum.edu.pk/jobs/).",
      "**TIMES University Multan (TUM)** invited applications from qualified academics in Southern Punjab for **Lecturer** and **Assistant Professor** appointments across five core teaching departments: **Law, Microbiology, Biochemistry, Economics, and Management Sciences**. With the **01 October 2026** submission deadline concluded, departmental selection committees conduct credential verification, micro-teaching demonstrations, and panel interviews.",
      "## Departmental Vacancies & Regulatory Eligibility Matrix",
      "| Department / Discipline | Advertised Ranks | Minimum Qualification & Statutory Standard |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Department of Law** | Assistant Professor, Lecturer | **LLM / PhD in Law** (18-year research degree in Law from an HEC-recognized university) + compliance with **HEC & Pakistan Bar Council (PBC) Legal Education Rules** (including bar enrollment/teaching experience benchmarks) |\n| **Microbiology & Biochemistry** | Assistant Professor, Lecturer | **PhD** (for Assistant Professor) or **MS / MPhil (18-year)** (for Lecturer) in Microbiology, Biochemistry, or Molecular Life Sciences with no 3rd Division in academic career |\n| **Management Sciences** | Assistant Professor, Lecturer | **PhD** or **MS / MPhil / 18-Year MBA** in Management, Finance, Marketing, or Supply Chain per HEC faculty appointment criteria |\n| **Economics** | Assistant Professor, Lecturer | **PhD** or **MS / MPhil in Economics** (18-year) from an HEC-recognized university |",
      "## Selection Process: Micro-Teaching Demo & HEC Scrutiny",
      "Candidates shortlisted by TIMES University Multan's Registrar and Dean offices are evaluated on both subject mastery and statutory HEC compliance:\n- **Transcript & Division Audit:** Under standard HEC faculty appointment rules, Lecturer candidates require a relevant 18-year MS/MPhil degree (minimum 3.00/4.00 CGPA or First Division) without any 3rd Division throughout their academic record.\n- **Law Faculty Bar Compliance:** Under Pakistan Bar Council Legal Education Rules, permanent Law faculty appointments require verified LLM/PhD credentials and prescribed legal practice or university teaching standing.\n- **Classroom Demonstration:** Shortlisted applicants deliver a structured 15-minute lecture before the Departmental Selection Committee assessing pedagogical clarity, board/slide organization, and research orientation.",
      "## Required Document File for University Faculty Interviews",
      "Keep original degrees and two attested photocopy sets ready for Registrar verification (review HEC attestation and equivalence steps in our [Official Documents Checklist Guide 2026](/jobs/government-jobs-documents-checklist-pakistan-2026)):\n- Updated academic CV listing HEC **HJRS-recognized publications** (if any) and thesis title.\n- Matric, Intermediate, BS/LLB, MS/MPhil/LLM, and PhD degrees and complete transcripts (with **HEC attestation stamps**).\n- Valid **NADRA CNIC**, Punjab/District **Domicile**, Bar Council license (for Law faculty), and experience/NOC letters from previous universities.",
      "## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)",
      "### Is the October 2026 faculty recruitment at TIMES University Multan still open?\nNo. The application window closed on **01 October 2026**. Academics in Punjab can monitor future semester openings directly at [tum.edu.pk/jobs/](https://www.tum.edu.pk/jobs/).",
      "### Where can MS/MPhil and PhD holders find other university teaching jobs?\nCompare private-sector faculty requirements in our [University of Lahore (UOL) Faculty Jobs Guide](/jobs/university-of-lahore-uol-jobs-2026) and browse live academic and corporate listings in [Private Sector Jobs in Pakistan](/category/private-jobs)."
    ],
