    "featuredImage": "/images/bahria-university-jobs-2026.webp",
    "imageAlt": "Bahria University Jobs 2026 Islamabad Karachi Lahore Faculty and Management Guide",
    "excerpt": "Bahria University recruits management officers, examination controllers, and academic faculty across its Islamabad (E-8/H-11), Karachi, and Lahore campuses via bahria.edu.pk/jobs. The October 12, 2026 cycle is now closed; review verified eligibility and official application procedures.",
    "content": [
      "## Recruitment Status Update (Verified October 19, 2026)\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Current Status — October 12, 2026 Advertisement Window Closed:**\n> The recruitment cycle advertised by **Bahria University** between September 28 and **October 12, 2026** has officially closed. Shortlisted applicants are notified directly by the Directorate of Human Resources for interviews. New campus-specific advertisements for Islamabad (E-8 & H-11), Karachi, and Lahore are published regularly on the official [Bahria University Jobs Noticeboard](https://www.bahria.edu.pk/jobs/) and [Online Job Portal](https://jobs.bahria.edu.pk/).",
      "## About Bahria University & Multi-Campus Structure\n\nEstablished by the Pakistan Navy in 2000 and chartered as a federally recognized degree-awarding institution, **Bahria University (BU)** operates major campuses across Pakistan:\n\n- **Head Office & Islamabad E-8 Campus:** Shangrila Road, Sector E-8, Islamabad (`+92-51-9260002`).\n- **Islamabad H-11 Engineering & Innovation Campus:** Sector H-11/4, Islamabad.\n- **Bahria University Karachi Campus (BUKC):** 13 National Stadium Road, Karachi (including Bahria University Health Sciences Campus at Sailor Street, DHA Phase-II, Karachi).\n- **Bahria University Lahore Campus (BULC):** 47-C, Civic Centre, Johar Town, Lahore.\n- **Institute of Professional Psychology (IPP):** Bahria Town / Stadium Road, Karachi.",
      "## Summary of Recent Advertised Cadres (Sept–Oct 2026 Cycle)\n\n| CADRE / DEPARTMENT | ADVERTISED DESIGNATIONS | QUALIFICATION & ACCREDITATION REQUIREMENTS |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Finance & Accounts Directorate** | Deputy Director Finance, Manager Accounts, Assistant Manager Finance | CA / ACMA / ACCA or MBA (Finance) / MS Finance from an HEC-recognized university with 5–10 years financial management & ERP experience |\n| **Examinations & Academics** | Deputy / Assistant Controller of Examinations, Academic Coordinator | MS / MBA / Master's degree (16–18 years education) with 3–7 years experience in semester examination rules and university CMS |\n| **Engineering & Computing Faculty** | Professor, Associate/Assistant Professor, Lecturer, Lab Engineer | PhD or MS/MPhil in CS, AI, Software, Electrical, or Mechanical Engineering per **HEC & PEC** regulations |\n| **Management, Law & Humanities** | Senior Assistant Professor, Assistant Professor, Lecturer | PhD or MS/MPhil/LLM in Business Administration, Supply Chain, Law, Media Studies, or Clinical Psychology |\n| **Health Sciences (BUHSC Karachi / Islamabad)** | Senior Registrar, Assistant Professor, Demonstrator, Nursing Instructor | MBBS / BDS / FCPS / MPhil / MSN with valid **PMDC** or **PNC** registration |",
      "## Mandatory HEC, PEC & PMDC Compliance Rules\n\nCandidates applying for teaching or administrative positions at Bahria University must ensure strict compliance with regulatory body standards:\n\n1. **HEC Equivalency for Foreign Degrees:** Applicants holding MS/MPhil or PhD degrees from overseas universities must attach an official **HEC Equivalence Certificate** verifying degree parity.\n2. **PEC Registration for Engineering Posts:** Candidates applying for Engineering faculty or Lab Engineer roles must hold an active **Pakistan Engineering Council (PEC)** registration number in the relevant engineering discipline.\n3. **PMDC / PNC Registration for Health Sciences:** Medical, dental, physical therapy, and nursing applicants at Bahria University Health Sciences Campuses must hold valid practicing licenses from the **Pakistan Medical and Dental Council (PMDC)** or **Pakistan Nursing Council (PNC)**.\n4. **Public Sector NOC Requirement:** Candidates currently serving in government, semi-government, or autonomous bodies must apply through proper channel and produce a formal **No Objection Certificate (NOC)** at the time of interview.",
      "## Official Two-Step Application Procedure at Bahria University\n\nBahria University enforces a structured application protocol through its Directorate of Human Resources:\n\n1. **Step 1 — Online Portal Submission:** Visit [jobs.bahria.edu.pk](https://jobs.bahria.edu.pk/) (or inspect active circulars at [bahria.edu.pk/jobs](https://www.bahria.edu.pk/jobs/)), register your candidate account, complete the online profile, and apply against the specific campus and designation.\n2. **Step 2 — Hard-Copy Dossier (Where Required by Notice):** Many Bahria University advertisements require applicants to also dispatch a **hard-copy application dossier** (containing a signed application form, detailed CV, attested copies of degrees/transcripts, CNIC, experience certificates, and photographs) via courier to the **Directorate of Human Resources, Bahria University Head Office, Shangrila Road, Sector E-8, Islamabad** (or the respective campus HR office) by the advertised closing date.\n3. **Shortlisting & TA/DA Policy:** Only shortlisted candidates are called for test/interview. No TA/DA is admissible for appearing in the selection process.",
      "## Fraud-Prevention & Official Verification Notice\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Verify Directly on `.edu.pk`:**\n> Bahria University never authorizes private placement agencies or social media recruiters to collect money. Always verify active job advertisements on [bahria.edu.pk/jobs](https://www.bahria.edu.pk/jobs/)."
    ],
