    "salary": "Consolidated Monetized Salary ~Rs. 132,000/Month (OG-2 Scale) + Central Bank Medical & Loan Benefits",
    "experience": "Fresh Graduates & Postgraduates Eligible (Max Age 26 Years; +3 Years Quota Relaxation)",
    "positions": "Assistant Director (OG-2) — State Bank Officer Training Scheme (SBOTS)",
    "lastDate": "2026-09-14",
    "noDeadline": false,
    "publishDate": "2026-09-26",
    "officialLink": "https://www.sbp.org.pk/careers/status.asp",
    "applyLink": "https://www.sbp.org.pk/careers/index.asp",
    "isVerified": true,
    "featured": false,
    "logoInitial": "SBP",
    "featuredImage": "/images/state-bank-officer-training-scheme-sbots-batch-27.webp",
    "imageAlt": "State Bank Officer Training Scheme SBOTS OG-2 Guide Verified Batch Status and Eligibility",
    "excerpt": "Comprehensive guide to the State Bank of Pakistan Officer Training Scheme (SBOTS) for Assistant Director (OG-2). Verify official batch statuses on sbp.org.pk/careers/status.asp (Batches 27 & 28 completed; Batch 29 closed Sept 14, 2026), academic criteria, age relaxation, and NIBAF training.",
    "content": [
      "## Official SBOTS Recruitment Status Verification (Verified October 19, 2026)\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Verified Status from State Bank of Pakistan ([sbp.org.pk/careers/status.asp](https://www.sbp.org.pk/careers/status.asp)):**\n> - **SBOTS 27th & 28th Batches:** Recruitment and induction processes are officially marked **Selection Completed** on the State Bank of Pakistan's recruitment status archive.\n> - **SBOTS 29th Batch (Assistant Director OG-2):** Online applications closed on **September 14, 2026**, and the competitive testing and selection stages are currently in progress.\n> - **No New SBOTS Batch Open Today:** Candidates should monitor [sbp.org.pk/careers/index.asp](https://www.sbp.org.pk/careers/index.asp) and [sbp.org.pk/careers/status.asp](https://www.sbp.org.pk/careers/status.asp) for the next official cycle announcement.",
      "## Overview of the State Bank Officer Training Scheme (SBOTS)\n\nThe **State Bank Officer Training Scheme (SBOTS)** is the flagship merit-based induction programme of the **State Bank of Pakistan (SBP)**—Pakistan's central bank—for recruiting entry-level **Assistant Directors (Officer Grade-2 / OG-2)**.\n\nSelected candidates undergo rigorous residential theoretical and applied central-banking training at the **National Institute of Banking and Finance (NIBAF)** in Islamabad before assuming permanent responsibilities across monetary policy, banking supervision, foreign exchange operations, financial stability, payment systems, and economic research at **SBP Head Office (I.I. Chundrigar Road, Karachi)** and field offices nationwide.",
      "## Verified Eligibility Criteria for SBOTS (Assistant Director OG-2)\n\nBased on official State Bank of Pakistan SBOTS recruitment notifications, candidates must fulfill the following academic and age requirements:\n\n| ELIGIBILITY PARAMETER | OFFICIAL SBP REQUIREMENT |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Eligible Disciplines** | Business Administration, Public Administration, Economics, Commerce, Finance, Accounting, Information Systems & Technology, Mathematics, Statistics, Human Resources, Law, Media/Communications, or Agriculture |\n| **Academic Qualification** | Minimum **16 years of education** (Master's or 4-year Bachelor's degree) from an **HEC-recognized** Pakistani university or an equivalent foreign degree with HEC equivalency |\n| **Minimum Marks / CGPA** | At least **60% aggregate marks** where percentage system applies, OR minimum **2.50 out of 4.00 CGPA** (or **3.50 out of 5.00 CGPA**) where GPA system applies |\n| **Maximum Age Limit** | **26 years** as of the closing date of applications |\n| **Age Relaxation Rules** | Upper age limit is relaxed by **3 years (up to 29 years)** for candidates holding valid domicile of **FATA/Merged Districts, Northern Areas (Gilgit-Baltistan), Balochistan, and Azad Jammu & Kashmir (AJK)**, and by **5 years (up to 31 years)** for current SBP employees fulfilling eligibility criteria |",
      "## Competitive Examination, Selection Stages & NIBAF Training\n\nInduction under SBOTS is strictly merit-based and follows provincial/regional quota allocations prescribed by the Federal Government:\n\n1. **Phase 1 — Written Recruitment Test:** Administered nationwide by SBP's designated testing agency, evaluating **English Comprehension & Composition**, **Quantitative & Analytical Reasoning**, and **Pakistan Economy, Current Affairs & General Knowledge**.\n2. **Phase 2 — Group Discussion & Psychometric Assessment:** Candidates qualifying the written cut-off are invited for group exercises and psychometric evaluations assessing leadership, policy analysis, and communication.\n3. **Phase 3 — Final Panel Interview:** Conducted by senior SBP executives across regional centers.\n4. **Phase 4 — Residential Training at NIBAF Islamabad:** Finalists join as **Trainee Assistant Directors (OG-2)** at the **National Institute of Banking and Finance (NIBAF), Sector H-8/1, Islamabad**, receiving classroom and central-banking rotational training prior to confirmation at SBP Karachi or SBP Banking Services Corporation (SBP-BSC) offices.",
      "## Compensation Package & Career Progression in OG-2\n\n- **Consolidated Monthly Emoluments:** Newly inducted Assistant Directors (OG-2) receive a consolidated monetized salary package of approximately **Rs. 132,000 per month** (revised periodically per SBP Board policy).\n- **Central Bank Perks & Benefits:** Comprehensive medical facility for self, spouse, children, and dependent parents; staff house-building, motor-car, and personal loan schemes; Contributory Provident Fund; and Gratuity.\n- **Foreign Higher Study Opportunities:** Confirmed SBP officers are eligible to compete for fully sponsored international Master's and PhD scholarships at leading global universities after completing mandatory service tenure.",
      "## Official State Bank of Pakistan Verification Portals\n\n- **Active SBP Career Notices:** [https://www.sbp.org.pk/careers/index.asp](https://www.sbp.org.pk/careers/index.asp)\n- **Official Recruitment Status Tracker:** [https://www.sbp.org.pk/careers/status.asp](https://www.sbp.org.pk/careers/status.asp)\n- **SBP Online Job Portal:** [https://career.sbp.org.pk/](https://career.sbp.org.pk/)\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Official Fee & Anti-Fraud Advisory:**\n> SBP only charges the nominal testing fee specified in official advertisements (typically Rs. 300–600 via authorized bank challan/1bill during active testing windows). Never pay third-party academies or individuals claiming guaranteed selection."
    ],
